  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only multiprofile with pca_n2000 and avgpool (config_002) is the clear best at 0.591 acc, while image-only resnet50 (config_010) is very weak at 0.208 acc. This raises the critical question of whether the image modality contains any complementary signal that can improve beyond the strong RNA baseline. Config_018 directly extends our best configuration by adding resnet50 image features via simple concatenation, the most standard and interpretable fusion. It is the most informative next step because: (1) it tests the single most important open question—whether multimodal fusion adds value over the best unimodal result; (2) concat is the simplest fusion, so if it fails to beat 0.591, we gain strong evidence that the image signal is too weak/noisy to be useful regardless of fusion strategy; (3) it uses the already-characterized resnet50 encoder, isolating the fusion question from encoder choice. Under a limited budget, this single experiment most efficiently reduces uncertainty about the core design decision of whether to pursue multimodal fusion at all."
}

